  "result": "The lock is in place across every write path in the spec. Full suite: 75 files and 632 tests pass. `tsc --noEmit` is clean, and ESLint reports nothing on the changed files.\n\nChoices I made where the spec left room:\n- **Invitation accept:** the lock is checked after the token checks (revoked, accepted, expired) and before the existing-member lookup. An already-member accepting into a locked workspace is refused too.\n- **Ordering:** in each write the lock comes right after `assertCan`, ahead of the archived, quota, and rate-limit guards, following the spec's rule.\n- **Banner:** only the `lockReason` field was added, so the shell has the data. I did not build the banner UI.\n- **Extra test files:** `tests/lib/billing-lock.test.ts` and `tests/services/workspace-lock.test.ts`. No existing test needed changing.",
